{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "07A5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{B}'), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{B}'})\n\\ar[r]_k \\ar[d]_{f'} &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{B}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{B}) \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}'), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}'})\n\\ar[r]^l \\ar[d]_{g'} &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\ar[d]^g \\\\\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}'), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{D}'})\n\\ar[r]^m &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}) \\\\\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "\\begin{align*}\nLm^* \\circ R(g \\circ f)_*\n& =\nLm^* \\circ Rg_* \\circ Rf_* \\\\\n& \\to Rg'_* \\circ Ll^* \\circ Rf_* \\\\\n& \\to Rg'_* \\circ Rf'_* \\circ Lk^* \\\\\n& = R(g' \\circ f')_* \\circ Lk^*\n\\end{align*}", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-base-change}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-compose-base-change}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:674edc576b14fb10b89f7ae44ff345674e6b09bc8db1b24aead204209b6e60bc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8fe340fa54634c242c7f21aec88db9ef8d2302033a844a1b69001e68d472a8ed", "source_text": "Consider a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nof ringed topoi. Then the base change maps of\nRemark <REF_0001>\nfor the two squares compose to give the base\nchange map for the outer rectangle. More precisely,\nthe composition\n<MATH_0002>\nis the base change map for the rectangle. We omit the verification.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8072588865fc1a3d4e6ac4a6c1368a439a7d6009edc766c1c536d84fcf3eb257", "unit_id": "tag:0E46:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "07A5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}''), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}''})\n\\ar[r]_{g'} \\ar[d]_{f''} &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}'), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}'})\n\\ar[r]_g \\ar[d]_{f'} &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}''), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{D}''})\n\\ar[r]^{h'} &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}'), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{D}'})\n\\ar[r]^h &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "\\begin{align*}\nL(h \\circ h')^* \\circ Rf_*\n& =\nL(h')^* \\circ Lh^* \\circ Rf_* \\\\\n& \\to L(h')^* \\circ Rf'_* \\circ Lg^* \\\\\n& \\to Rf''_* \\circ L(g')^* \\circ Lg^* \\\\\n& = Rf''_* \\circ L(g \\circ g')^*\n\\end{align*}", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-base-change}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-compose-base-change-horizontal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:74e83caf10343b1835bacd656b22f9ba0bdb5ff73a5f978b07999cee2d38032a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6ca84b92c2ae11ebf21b49e94a6aa1de972d259109a4d30effad2da80e6c721b", "source_text": "Consider a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nof ringed topoi. Then the base change maps of\nRemark <REF_0001>\nfor the two squares compose to give the base\nchange map for the outer rectangle. More precisely,\nthe composition\n<MATH_0002>\nis the base change map for the rectangle. We omit the verification.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8072588865fc1a3d4e6ac4a6c1368a439a7d6009edc766c1c536d84fcf3eb257", "unit_id": "tag:0E47:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07A5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nLf^*f_*\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\nf^*f_*\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\ar[d] \\\\\nLf^*Rf_*\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet\n}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$Lf^* \\to f^*$", "MATH_0006": "$f_* \\to Rf_*$", "MATH_0007": "$Lf^* \\circ Rf_* \\to \\text{id}$", "MATH_0008": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-adjoints-push-pull-compatibility}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b035994203405732d477b36e1b5fdeea343251355bd0d754d4a673cf13bb035", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b6404bc4037b8f5e9923f63886e20ab6e19a65ebdc2ffa404186e4b1a2518a9f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of ringed topoi.\nLet <MATH_0002>\nbe a complex of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nThe diagram\n<MATH_0004>\ncoming from <MATH_0005> on complexes, <MATH_0006> on complexes,\nand adjunction <MATH_0007>\ncommutes in <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf002b4da105d5d8dcb12a863959b074f59d5e9f8de14d125bb17c10b6f2863f", "unit_id": "tag:0FPI:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07A5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Q}^\\bullet \\to f_*\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{Q}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{P}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{P}^\\bullet \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\nf_*\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{Q}^\\bullet \\ar[r] & f_*\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet\n}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{P}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{P}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0012": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nf^*\\mathcal{P}^\\bullet \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\nf^*f_*\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\ar[d] \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\ar[d] \\\\\nf^*\\mathcal{Q}^\\bullet \\ar[r] &\nf^*f_*\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet\n}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-K-flat-resolution}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-derived-base-change}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-K-flat}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2b4c6eee0f4d71335d44d16b007d1544ecc78037d6c623ab4c50ca49df547280", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ac54cd4ea896ae334aa652bda1cd7986d85428eaf35253278e5ce6f4a4e9f504", "source_text": "We will use the existence of K-flat resolutions and\nK-injective resolutions, see Lemmas\n<REF_0001>, <REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003> and the discussion above.\nChoose a quasi-isomorphism\n<MATH_0001> where <MATH_0002>\nis K-injective as a complex of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nChoose a quasi-isomorphism <MATH_0004>\nwhere <MATH_0005> is a K-flat complex of\n<MATH_0006>-modules with flat terms.\nWe can choose a K-flat complex of\n<MATH_0007>-modules <MATH_0008> with flat terms\nand a diagram of morphisms of complexes\n<MATH_0009>\ncommutative up to homotopy where the top horizontal arrow\nis a quasi-isomorphism. Namely, we can first choose such a\ndiagram for some complex <MATH_0010> because\nthe quasi-isomorphisms form a multiplicative system in\nthe homotopy category of complexes and then we can choose\na resolution of <MATH_0011> by a K-flat complex with flat terms.\nTaking pullbacks we obtain a diagram of morphisms of complexes\n<MATH_0012>\ncommutative up to homotopy. The outer rectangle witnesses the\ntruth of the statement in the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:12cdea2468228fb7229bdadb62534bd3434ef2ec160101f645062012bc67bf9a", "unit_id": "tag:0FPI:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "07A5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$Lf^*$", "MATH_0003": "$Rf_*$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nRf_*K \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}}^\\mathbf{L} Rf_*L\n\\longrightarrow\nRf_*(K \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}}^\\mathbf{L} L)\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0006": "$K, L$", "MATH_0007": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0008": "$Lf^*(Rf_*K \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}}^\\mathbf{L} Rf_*L) \\to\nK \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}}^\\mathbf{L} L$", "MATH_0009": "$Lf^*(Rf_*K \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}}^\\mathbf{L} Rf_*L) =\nLf^*Rf_*K \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}}^\\mathbf{L} Lf^*Rf_*L$", "MATH_0010": "$Lf^*Rf_*K \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}}^\\mathbf{L} Lf^*Rf_*L\n\\to K \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}}^\\mathbf{L} L$", "MATH_0011": "$Lf^* \\circ Rf_* \\to \\text{id}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-tensor-product}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-cup-product}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6d517b6cb4855285540647b2a5527f2f05c8c8ceb3c44d120d056579a032b007", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b2218e358157c0b03892ec64cc6dc5be37ae721cb12fef1815fdb6e9af0a96c4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of\nringed topoi. The adjointness of <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> allows us to construct\na relative cup product\n<MATH_0004>\nin <MATH_0005> for all <MATH_0006> in <MATH_0007>.\nNamely, this map is adjoint to a map\n<MATH_0008> for which we can take the\ncomposition of the isomorphism\n<MATH_0009>\n(Lemma <REF_0001>)\nwith the map\n<MATH_0010>\ncoming from the counit <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3c83e479b319c2d51668bd1fe7a4491dbe3ae5f7a869b0812ccc4edb789ffa7f", "unit_id": "tag:0B6C:statement"}
